ts, visually demonstrating the XOR operation: an orange arrow points from t=
he top bit to the bottom bit if the top bit is 1, and a light-blue arrow po=
ints from the bottom bit to the top bit if the bottom bit is 1. The result =
of the XOR operation (A XOR B) is implicitly shown by the arrangement of th=
e arrows, where the presence of an arrow indicates a '1' result and its abs=
ence indicates a '0' result.  The pattern repeats across all positions, ill=
ustrating the consistent application of the XOR operation on each bit pair.=
" loading=3D"lazy" width=3D"303" height=3D"93" decoding=3D"async" data-nimg=
=3D"1" style=3D"color:transparent" src=3D"https://bytebytego.com/images/cou=
