QKLL25QR.svg?dpl=3Ddpl_CEjisbLnWxFQGUTRjiHGoKY1oV5c"></div></figure>
<p>This suggests that if we had a way to extract all the even and odd-posit=
ioned bits separately, we could shift them accordingly and then merge them =
back together, so the odd-positioned bits are in the even positions, and vi=
ce versa.</p>
<figure class=3D"py-1"><div style=3D"display:flex;justify-content:center"><=
